main.go:583-595: lexical containment holds, but C:\proj\CON, NUL, AUX, PRN, COM1 (and aux.h-style names on Win10) are device paths; CreateFileW opens them regardless of the directory prefix and Go's os package does nothing about them. read_file path=CON blocks on console input and steals the agent's keystrokes in window mode; write_file path=NUL 'succeeds' and writes nothing; write_file path=Source/aux.h targets a serial device. Windows-only, unverified from Linux. Related: #49 (symlinks).
Acceptance: reject !filepath.IsLocal(rel) before joining (Go >= 1.20, CI uses 1.22) -- it also covers .. and absolute paths in one place; settle by trying read_file path=CON on Windows; test on both platforms.
